      "comment": "When `globalsList` is empty, `globalsList.map(escapeKeys).join('|')` produces the empty string `''`, and `new RegExp('')` is a universal-match regex that matches any code string. Every file then passes the code filter and enters the handler, where `globalsList.every(...)` on an empty array returns `true` and immediately bails out with `return undefined`. This entirely defeats the performance purpose of the code filter (the optimization that justifies this PR) whenever `externals` happens to be an empty object. Guard against this case before constructing the regex:\n\n```ts\nconst globalsCodeFilter = globalsList.length > 0\n  ? new RegExp(globalsList.map(escapeKeys).join('|'))\n  : null;\n```\n\nAnd then conditionally apply `filter: { code: globalsCodeFilter }` only when the filter is non-null (or omit the `filter` key entirely for the empty case)."
